# Loop pack disambiguation — prefer loops-*

When a task matches a skill name that exists in both the `loops` pack and the Hermes built-in pack, **always prefer the `loops-*` version**. The Hermes copies at `hermes-*` are kept for reference but should not auto-fire.

## Name map

| Intent | Use (preferred) | Available as fallback |
|---|---|---|
| Plan + implement a feature | `loops-plan-and-implement` | `hermes-plan-and-implement` |
| Test-driven dev | `loops-tdd` | `hermes-tdd` (currently `test-driven-development`) |
| Spec → Attack → Repair | `loops-sar` | `hermes-sar` |
| Meta-router | `loops-use-the-loop` | `hermes-use-the-loop` |
| Adversarial review / pre-merge | `loops-adversarial-gate` | `hermes-adversarial-loop` (different framing) |

## Why

The `loops` repo at `~/code/loops` is the canonical workflow definition going forward. Hermes's built-in versions are the previous implementation. Both are technically functional; the `loops-` versions are better maintained and aligned with the global install.

## When the Hermes version is appropriate

- The user explicitly says "use the Hermes version" or names a Hermes-specific feature (e.g. "the persona system in sar")
- A `loops-*` skill fails to load and the user needs the Hermes fallback
- The user is in a context that doesn't have the loops global install wired

## Trigger phrase routing

| User says | Action |
|---|---|
| "use the loops" / "loops?" | Read `~/.loops/dispatcher/loop.md` and follow it (this finds the `loops-*` skill) |
| "plan-and-implement" / "implement X" | Load `loops-plan-and-implement` |
| "tdd" / "write tests first" | Load `loops-tdd` |
| "sar" / "spec attack repair" | Load `loops-sar` |
| "use the loop" / "smallest composition" | Load `loops-use-the-loop` |
| "adversarial review" / "red team this" | Load `loops-adversarial-gate` |

## What NOT to do

- Don't load both `loops-plan-and-implement` and `hermes-plan-and-implement` for the same task — pick one
- Don't mention the disambiguation to the user unless they ask which version is running
- Don't auto-fall-back to Hermes-* if loops-* is unavailable — report the missing skill and ask the user how to proceed
